From 371cbf953f4d4e76cec0ad12f55a86039da74172 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:25:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rules: MM6's stat effect table (two src/ui assertions left
 old)

The statistic effect table is MM6's (MM6-GAPS.md 3, GF-M): 0 -> -6, 3 ->
-5, 5 -> -4, 7 -> -3, 9 -> -2, 11 -> -1, 13 -> 0, 15 -> +1, 17 -> +2,
19 -> +3, 21 -> +4, 25 -> +5, 30 -> +6, 35 -> +7, 40 -> +8, 50 -> +9,
+1 per 25 to 300 -> +19, 350 -> +20, 400 -> +25, 500 -> +30. Was one
step too high from 4 to 399 (11-12 gave 0) and +22 / +23 at 400 / 500.
Screenshot-21's level-1 Paladin now comes out: Attack +2, Damage 5-11,
Shoot +1, SP 7, AC 14 (his 31 HP still do not: the class table, left to
the owner).

Tests: new stats.test.ts with the whole table; combat.test.ts's stat
test, and character.test.ts, creation.test.ts and party.test.ts, encoded
the old table; updated to MM6's values, with GF-M's recovery example
(99) and screenshot-21's Paladin.

NOT GREEN: two src/ui assertions encode the old table and fail with this
commit: src/ui/creation-model.test.ts expects Might 17 -> bonus 3 (MM6:
2) and src/ui/sheet-model.test.ts expects Might 32 -> 7 (MM6: 6). The
coordinator agreed to changing just those two values, but the permission
system denied my edit to src/ui, so they are left for the owner: update
them, or drop this commit (it is last and self-contained).

DESIGN 14.1 and src/game/README.md updated; decision log line extended.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5BePXiaXkqzr4br9g7qBv
